{"id":"champs-elysees","name":"Champs-Élysées","place":"Paris, France","kind":"loop","source":"Route: classic 2013-2023 Tour de France final-stage circuit, routed on OpenStreetMap geometry (Overpass API, ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) with a custom shortest path through ~30 waypoints (one-ways ignored; single OSM centreline of the Champs used in both directions). Direction follows the published description (fr/en Wikipedia \"Étape des Champs-Élysées\": hairpin via Cours la Reine onto the riverside Voie Georges-Pompidou, Général-Lemonnier tunnel, Rue de Rivoli back to Concorde) and OSM traffic flow. Lap from the finish (Champs-Élysées westbound at Av. Winston-Churchill/Av. de Marigny, by the Petit Palais): up the Champs-Élysées via Rond-Point Marcel-Dassault - counter-clockwise round Place Charles de Gaulle (Arc de Triomphe) - down the Champs-Élysées - Place de la Concorde (SW side) - Cours la Reine - hairpin onto Voie Georges-Pompidou (underpass beneath the Concorde/Pont de la Concorde approach) - Quai des Tuileries - Quai Aimé Césaire - Avenue du Général-Lemonnier (tunnel under the Carrousel gardens) - Place des Pyramides - Rue de Rivoli (W) - Place de la Concorde (N side) - Champs-Élysées to finish. Elevation: IGN RGE ALTI (1 m DTM) via Géoplateforme altimetry API (data.geopf.fr/altimetrie/1.0/calcul/alti/rest/elevation.json, resource ign_rge_alti_wld), sampled every ~12.5 m; tunnel correction: Voie Georges-Pompidou 4290-4352 m (DEM surface up to 34.6 m replaced by 29.26->29.64 m); Avenue du Général Lemonnier 5228-5403 m (DEM surface up to 35.24 m replaced by 30.51->30.15 m); cross-checked with EU-DEM 25 m via OpenTopoData (eudem25m, surface-model noise from trees/buildings, lap climb 70 m so not used). Smoothing: 62 m rolling median + 75 m centred moving average, resampled to ~25 m; grade cap 22% per 25 m step (applied to 0 steps).","lapMeters":7016.3,"climbMeters":35.2,"points":[[0.0,32.75,48.867754,2.313963],[25.0,32.7,48.867853,2.313657],[49.9,32.64,48.